 ## Overview
-The VolumePro 500 is a specialized hardware architecture for high-performance volume rendering, based on the Cube-4 design [S3, S4, unofficial]. It implements the shear-warp algorithm using true trilinear interpolation and dedicated hardware for gradient estimation, classification, and Phong shading [S3, S4, unofficial]. Unlike its predecessor Cube-3, which used global connectivity for compositing, VolumePro 500 employs simple local interconnections and accumulating compositors, allowing for easy scalability and direct memory-to-pipeline connectivity [S3, S4, unofficial]. It solves the problem of real-time rendering of large volumetric datasets (up to $1024^3$ voxels) by maximizing memory throughput through 3D skewing and parallel processing of ray groups [S3, S4, unofficial].
+The VolumePro 500 is a specialized hardware architecture for high-performance volume rendering, based on the Cube-4 design [S3, S4, unofficial]. It implements the shear-warp algorithm using true trilinear interpolation and dedicated hardware for gradient estimation, classification, and Phong shading [S3, S4, unofficial]. Based on the Cube-4 architecture, it employs simple local interconnections and accumulating compositors, contrasting with Cube-3's global connectivity and binary compositing tree [S3, S4, unofficial]. It solves the problem of real-time rendering of large volumetric datasets (up to $256^3$ voxels at 30 fps, with the underlying architecture scalable to $1024^3$ via software partitioning) by maximizing memory throughput through 3D skewing and parallel processing of ray groups [S3, S4, unofficial].
 
